{%- comment -%}
  Mirrors ../design-system/src/react/Form/Form.tsx -- the column that spaces a form's fields apart.

  Form.tsx is `<form>` wrapping `<Box gap="lg">`. This snippet is only the Box half, and that is
  deliberate: on a Shopify storefront the <form> element itself is emitted by Liquid's {% form %}
  tag, which owns the action URL, the CSRF token and the form_type field. So callers render
  {% form %} themselves and put this immediately inside it -- the resulting DOM is the same
  form > div > fields that Form.tsx produces.

  Accepts:
    content     Required. The fields' markup, built with {% capture %} before rendering.
    class       Extra classes.
    attributes  Raw string appended to the wrapper tag.
    gap         Optional CSS length (e.g. "24px"), overriding the column's gap between fields.
                Defaults to --space-lg, Form.tsx's own `<Box gap="lg">` value. Additive: a caller
                that passes nothing renders byte-identical to before this param existed.
    validate    Pass true to show client-side validation errors in the design system's own markup
                instead of the browser's native bubble. Wraps the column in
                <mionas-form-validation> and loads assets/mionas-form-validation.js, which sets
                `novalidate` on the surrounding form and writes the same classes and message
                paragraph that a server-side `error` param produces.

                OPT-IN, not the default. blocks/mionas-form.liquid is the third caller of this
                snippet and composes arbitrary child field blocks, so the two error messages below
                cannot be assumed to fit it. Turn it on there only when someone asks.

  Usage:
    {% capture form_fields %}
      {% render 'mionas-text-field', label: 'Email', name: 'contact[email]', id: 'x-email', type: 'email' %}
    {% endcapture %}
    {% form 'contact' %}
      {% render 'mionas-form', content: form_fields %}
    {% endform %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign form_classes = 'mionas-form'
  if class
    assign form_classes = form_classes | append: ' ' | append: class
  endif
%}
{%- capture form_column -%}
  <div
    class="{{ form_classes }}"
    {% if gap %}style="--mionas-form-gap: {{ gap }};"{% endif %}
    {{ attributes }}
  >{{ content }}</div>
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if validate -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The messages are literals, not schema settings: blocks/mionas-email-signup.liquid's header
    records why merchant-settable error copy was rejected, and the same reasoning holds here.

    Both current callers have exactly one required field and it is the email, so the copy names it.
    A form with some other required field passes data-message-required on that input itself, via
    snippets/mionas-text-field.liquid's `attributes` param -- the per-input value wins.

    The script tag repeats per form instance, which is fine: the browser dedupes a module by URL and
    the customElements.define in the asset is guarded. Same pattern as blocks/popup-link.liquid
    loading dialog.js.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Carries a class as well as its tag name so the stylesheet below can select it the way every
    other rule in this theme selects things. Nothing depends on the tag being styleable.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <mionas-form-validation
    class="mionas-form-validation"
    data-message-required="Escribe tu email."
    data-message-invalid="Escribe un email válido."
  >
    {{ form_column }}
  </mionas-form-validation>
  <script src="{{ 'mionas-form-validation.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>
{%- else -%}
  {{ form_column }}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Form.tsx's <Box gap="lg">. --space-lg is what Box's gap="lg" resolves to, and is the fallback
     when a caller passes no `gap` -- see the `gap` param above. */
  .mionas-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
    gap: var(--mionas-form-gap, var(--space-lg));
  }

  /* `display: contents` is load-bearing, not tidiness. An unstyled custom element is `inline`, and
     this one sits between the form and .mionas-form -- which is exactly the chain
     blocks/mionas-email-signup.liquid's inline layout reaches through to flip .mionas-form to a
     row. Generating no box at all keeps that layout byte-for-byte what it was before validation
     was added. */
  .mionas-form-validation {
    display: contents;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
